proxmox-kernel-7.3 (7.3.6-1+s390x2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * KVM: s390: vsie: rewind the PSW of nested guests in ESA mode in the
    right format, so that an instruction vsie wants repeated (for
    example the first STORE FACILITY LIST EXTENDED after entry into SIE)
    is no longer skipped; with a selftest.
  * build with a fixed build user and host name: the version banner of
    7.3.6-1+s390x1 named the account and machine it was built on.

 -- Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:39:04 +0000

proxmox-kernel-7.3 (7.3.6-1+s390x1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * s390x port: build for IBM Z (s390x), booted through zipl.
  * s390x: kernel config based on the Debian s390x config of the 7.3 series
    plus the common Proxmox overrides; additionally enable vfio-ccw, vfio-ap,
    protected key support and kexec.
  * s390x: no dependency on pve-firmware, no signed-template package and no
    Rust build dependencies.

 -- Yvan Janssens <yvanj@cyber.gent>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:30:41 +0000

